            <ArticleTitle>The management of the cardiac patient requiring noncardiac surgery. Preoperative evaluation and management of the surgical patient with heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>985-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When a patient has coronary artery disease, congestive heart failure, or a prosthetic heart valve, what steps must the surgeon take to prepare the patient for noncardiac surgery? The author succinctly addresses the merits of several treatments for these groups of patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
